# The unclosed `(` is reported where it opens, even lines away from where the input ends.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv'
| where (amount > 10
| take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..48
  PIPELINE@0..47
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 "\n"
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..47
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      PAREN_EXPR@26..47
        L_PAREN@26..27 "("
        PIPELINE@27..47
          BIN_EXPR@27..38
            NAME_REF@27..33
              IDENT@27..33 "amount"
            WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
            GT@34..35 ">"
            WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
            LITERAL@36..38
              LONG@36..38 "10"
          WHITESPACE@38..39 "\n"
          PIPE@39..40 "|"
          WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
          TAKE_OP@41..47
            IDENT@41..45 "take"
            WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
            LITERAL@46..47
              LONG@46..47 "5"
  WHITESPACE@47..48 "\n"

error[DS0112]: unclosed `(`
  --> query:2:9
  |
2 | | where (amount > 10
  |         ^ this `(` is never closed
3 | | take 5
  |         - the input ends before a `)`
  |
  = help: add `)` where the bracketed part ends
